    "description": "PARKED — fully additive. Nothing in the base build needs to change to accommodate it later.\n\nWhat the base build gives you: each deal carries its current sync status and the message from its most recent attempt. Salesforce field history will show THAT a deal moved in and out of Failed, but for LONG TEXT FIELDS IT DOES NOT RETAIN PREVIOUS VALUES. If a deal fails Monday with one error and again Thursday with a different one, Thursday overwrites Monday.\n\nDay to day that is fine — Ops needs to know what is broken now. It matters only for cross-time questions: which errors are most common, whether a particular operator's deals fail repeatedly, whether the failure rate changed after a CMS release, how long failures take to clear.\n\nProposed solution:\n\n* A dedicated integration error log object, DELIBERATELY GENERIC rather than deal-specific, so it serves any Salesforce object pushing to any external system\n\n* One record per attempt: source object and record, target system, direction, event type, outcome, HTTP status, request and response detail, timestamp, retry count\n\n* Retention policy so data does not accumulate indefinitely\n\n* A standard set of reports\n\nEffort 12-20h INDICATIVE ONLY — not scoped in detail; would be scoped as separate work. Grows in value as SF-CMS touchpoints increase beyond deal publishing.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §4.5, D10.",
